From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mfplat: Return E_NOTIMPL from a memory 2D buffer's GetService again.

A 2D buffer in memory answers IMFGetService::GetService with E_NOTIMPL
again, as Windows does: the evr tests (which run on Windows) get E_NOTIMPL
for MR_BUFFER_SERVICE from the memory buffers of a sample allocator without
a device manager. Patch 2830 had changed it to MF_E_UNSUPPORTED_SERVICE,
which made that evr test fail.

Gate: test/mfplat-buffers-gate.sh (2830's gate, now expecting E_NOTIMPL).
---
 dlls/mfplat/buffer.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/mfplat/buffer.c b/dlls/mfplat/buffer.c
index b2b2c73..7097088 100644
--- a/dlls/mfplat/buffer.c
+++ b/dlls/mfplat/buffer.c
@@ -895,11 +895,17 @@ static ULONG WINAPI memory_2d_buffer_gs_Release(IMFGetService *iface)
     return IMFMediaBuffer_Release(&buffer->IMFMediaBuffer_iface);
 }
 
+/* A buffer in memory has no surface to give: Windows answers E_NOTIMPL here
+ * (evr tests: a sample allocator without a device manager makes such buffers,
+ * and MR_BUFFER_SERVICE on them returns E_NOTIMPL). */
 static HRESULT WINAPI memory_2d_buffer_gs_GetService(IMFGetService *iface, REFGUID service, REFIID riid, void **obj)
 {
     TRACE("%p, %s, %s, %p.\n", iface, debugstr_guid(service), debugstr_guid(riid), obj);
 
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_MEM2D_SERVICE_UNSUPPORTED
     return MF_E_UNSUPPORTED_SERVICE;
+#endif
+    return E_NOTIMPL;
 }
 
 static const IMFGetServiceVtbl memory_2d_buffer_gs_vtbl =
